.TH FANDYND 8 "2026-10-22" "fandyn 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fandynd \- calibrated low-noise fan control daemon for Jetson Nano
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fandynd
.br
.B fandynd \-\-check
.br
.B fandynd status
.br
.B fandynd \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fandynd
drives the pwm-fan of a Jetson Nano from the fixed profile written by
.BR fandyn-calibrate (8).
Once per second it reads the hottest CPU/GPU thermal zone and writes
.IR /sys/devices/pwm-fan/target_pwm .
It speeds up immediately, slows down only after the board has cooled by the
calibrated hysteresis, stops the fan when cool (zero-RPM) and starts it with
a verified kick.
.PP
It runs the fan at full speed when the temperature is critical, when no sensor
can be read for 3 seconds, and when the fan does not spin after 3 kicks.
It takes fan control back if the kernel re-enables its own, keeps running if
the fan device disappears, and falls back to a built-in safe profile when the
profile is missing or corrupt. On SIGTERM it hands the fan back to the kernel.
SIGHUP reloads the profile; an invalid profile is rejected and the current one kept.
.PP
It uses no heap memory and no floating point, and is normally started by systemd
.RI ( fandyn.service ,
with a watchdog).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Show the profile, sensors, fan and curve, then exit.
.TP
.B status
Show the live state (temperature, PWM, RPM, mode).
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " FILE, " \-\-root " DIR, " \-\-run\-dir " DIR, " \-\-tick\-ms " N"
Testing only: alternative profile, sysfs root, runtime directory and tick.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/fandyn/profile
Fixed profile (CRC-protected) written by fandyn-calibrate.
.TP
.I /run/fandyn/status
Live state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fandyn-calibrate (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
